      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to the [[credential-scoping]] page, the Anthropic API key is **injected into the environment of the spawned child process**, immediately before that process starts. \n\nThe key details are:\n\n- The key is **not** held in the Hub process\u0027s own environment\n- A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n- The key is injected **only into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process** (and similarly for the Query agent)\n- The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated\n- This means if the Hub process is compromised, the attacker cannot leak the credential by inspecting the Hub\u0027s environment variables\u2014the key exists only inside the short-lived child process",
